<title>UK: RTZ shares fall on profit-taking, CRA fall.</title>
<headline>RTZ shares fall on profit-taking, CRA fall.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in RTZ fell 14 pence to 965 due to profit-taking on Tuesday triggered by an overnight drop in CRA shares, market makers said.</p>
<p>&quot;CRA was the prime mover,&quot; said one. &quot;That triggered some arbitrage selling.&quot;</p>
<p>CRA, which closed down 18 cents at A$20.00, is the Australian arm of mining giant RTZ-CRA.</p>
<p>Shares in RTZ have been in an upward trend since November 13 when they closed at 921. Helped by a firm copper price, the shares had moved up in a straight line to peak at 918 on November 22.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
